/*
 * Declares the MapIteratorEndValue class.
 *
 * MapIteratorEndValue represents a test on a map iterator to determine whether
 * it has reached the end of the iteration. The operator evaluates to `true`
 * when the iterator still points to a valid entry, and to `false` when the
 * iterator has reached the terminal position.
 *
 * This check is used internally by map iteration constructs to control loop
 * termination.
 *
 * <hr>
 *
 * @Package: ymirc
 * @Module: ymirc::semantic::generator::value::operator::map::iteration::end
 * @File: ymirc/semantic/generator/value/operator/map/iteration/end.yr
 * @Author(s):
 *   - Emile Cadorel <ecadorel@gmail.com>
 *
 * @Created(YYYY-MM-DD): 2024-11-15
 * @Copyright(C) 2021–2026 GNU-Ymir
 * @License
 *   ```text
